  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This dish uses two ingredients unique to the Rajasthani desert: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ker ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ker"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", small tart dried berries, and "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "sangri ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sangri"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", long dried beans from local trees. Together they form a dry "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "sabzi",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "sabzi"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " with a distinctive tangy flavour. Both ingredients require overnight soaking."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ker and sangri are available at Indian grocery shops. If ker is unavailable, substitute capers preserved in brine, rinsed well. The texture differs but the tartness is similar."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
